stream
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 726 Td (7. Alarms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 704 Td (Factory default set points for the HX-220:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 683 Td (Gas | Low alarm | High alarm | STEL | TWA) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 671 Td (H2S | 5 ppm | 15 ppm | 15 ppm | 5 ppm) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 659 Td (CO | 35 ppm | 200 ppm | 200 ppm | 30 ppm) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 647 Td (LEL \(CH4\) | 10% LEL | 25% LEL | n/a | n/a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 635 Td (O2 | 19.5% vol \(falling\) | 23.5% vol \(rising\) | n/a | n/a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 613 Td (Note that the HX-220 defaults differ from the HX-210 \(H2S high 10 ppm, CO low 30 ppm and high) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 600 Td (100 ppm, LEL high 20% LEL, O2 high 23.0% vol\). Sites running mixed fleets should align set) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 587 Td (points in Meridian Link to avoid confusion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 565 Td (Low, high, STEL, TWA and over-range alarms behave as described for the HX-210: low alarms are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 552 Td (non-latching by default, high alarms latch until acknowledged in clean air, STEL and TWA alarms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 539 Td (cannot be acknowledged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 517 Td (When Bluetooth is connected, every gas alarm, man-down alarm and panic alarm is sent to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 504 Td (paired Meridian Link Mobile app, together with the GPS position, within 5 seconds.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 479 Td (8. Man-down and panic alarms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 457 Td (The man-down function detects that the wearer has stopped moving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 435 Td (1. If the instrument detects no motion for the man-down timer \(default 60 seconds\), it enters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 422 Td (   a pre-alarm: a slow beep and "MOVE?" on the display.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 409 Td (2. The pre-alarm lasts 15 seconds. Any movement or a press of ON/OK cancels it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 396 Td (3. If not cancelled, a full man-down alarm sounds and is transmitted with the GPS position.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 383 Td (The man-down timer can be set between 30 and 180 seconds in Menu > Supervisor > Lone Worker >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 370 Td (No-Motion Time. The pre-alarm period is fixed at 15 seconds. Man-down can be disabled only by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 357 Td (the supervisor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 335 Td (The panic alarm is triggered by holding the red PANIC button for 2 seconds. It is always) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 322 Td (latching.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 297 Td (9. Bluetooth and GPS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 275 Td (The HX-220 pairs with the Meridian Link Mobile app on Android 11 or later and iOS 16 or later.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 262 Td (To pair, select Menu > Wireless > Pair, then scan the six-digit code shown on the display from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 249 Td (the app. The instrument remembers one paired phone at a time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 227 Td (GPS positions are logged every 60 seconds in the datalog. Indoors, where no fix is available,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 214 Td (the last known position is sent with an alarm and marked as stale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 192 Td (If the Bluetooth module fails its self-test the instrument shows E-131 \(Bluetooth module) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 179 Td (fault\). Gas detection continues normally. Error E-131 applies to the HX-220 only.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 154 Td (10. Optional sampling pump HX-PMP-22) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 132 Td (The HX-PMP-22 clips to the front of the HX-220 over the sensor grille and draws a sample at 0.5) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 119 Td (L/min. It allows pre-entry testing of confined spaces with sample tubing up to 30 m long. Allow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 106 Td (2 seconds per metre of tubing plus 60 seconds for the reading to stabilise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 84 Td (The pump is detected automatically. If flow falls below 0.3 L/min \(for example if the inlet is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 71 Td (blocked or the tube is kinked\) the instrument shows E-113 \(pump flow fault\) and sounds the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 58 Td (fault tone. Clear the blockage and press ON/OK. Test the pump block alarm daily by covering the) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 3 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 8 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R >> >> >>
